  "id": "oyelarans",
  "neon": "#ff5a3c",
  "note": "OYELARAN'S — the noodle bar, which had no model of its own either and resolved to the shared\n`type:noodle_bar` arm.\n\nIts architecture is one idea: the ground floor is not a room. It is a counter under the building,\nopen to the pavement, with three storeys of flats over it on two posts. Neither renderer here can\ncut a hole in a wall, so the ground floor is SET BACK and the block above OVERHANGS it — which is\nthe same building from the street, and is literally what an arcade shophouse is.\n\n⚠ THE POSTS ARE STRUCTURE, NOT DECORATION. An overhanging box with nothing under its leading edge\nreads as a mistake from every angle that can see under it, and this is a frontage a truck cab sits\nlevel with. Two square posts at the front corners carry it, which is both true and cheap.\n\n⚠ THE FLATS ABOVE HAVE BALCONIES AND THE BALCONIES CLAIM `stair`. `SECTION_OF` maps `balcony` to\nthe same section as a fire escape, so authoring these keeps the derived kit out of it — and\nbalconies hung with somebody's washing over a food counter is the building, where a steel escape\nwould be a different one.",
  "pal": "ty_broth",
